course: dictionary
lesson: 406
title: Applause and what it tells us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Applause is the sound of many people clapping their hands. People clap to show they enjoyed something or agree with it. The word can also mean praise or approval, which is good opinion, even when there is no noise at all.
explain: Read the words around it. «Sports teams often wear black armbands or hold a minute's silence or applause to show respect and support.» Applause sits next to silence, which means no sound at all. The two are a pair: one quiet and one loud, both shown as respect.
explain: Look for the clues: a crowd, a stage, a finish line. In a story, phrases like «a round of applause» or «loud applause» tell the reader that something went well. You may not know the word yet, but the place and the people tell you what is happening.
fact: Applause means the sound of people clapping their hands.
fact: Applause can also mean praise or approval.
fact: Applause is uncountable, so you say «a round of applause», not «an applause» for each clap.
fact: «Thunderous applause» means very loud clapping.
fact: Sports teams can show respect with a minute's silence or with applause.
exercise: What is applause? | A loud shout of anger | A long, quiet pause in a play | *Clapping hands to show enjoyment or agreement | Sudden rain on a tin roof
exercise: «Sports teams often wear black armbands or hold a minute's silence or applause to show respect and support.» What does the applause show? | *Respect and support | That the game is over for today | That the teams are hungry | Anger at the other team
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that means a pause with no sound. | respect | armbands | *silence | teams
exercise: The whole hall clapped for the choir for a long time. What did the hall give the choir? | A shout of anger | Thunder | Silence | *Applause
exercise: Which phrase means very loud clapping? | Quiet silence | Gentle applause | *Thunderous applause | A minute's silence
test: Mia's poem won a prize, and the class clapped and cheered. What does the clapping show? | That the lesson is over for the day | That the class is lost | *Praise and approval | Anger and boredom
test: Which word is a pair with the word silence in the sports sentence? | *Applause | Armbands | Support | Teams
exam: Which best describes applause? | Only a kind of silence | *Praise or approval, and also the sound of clapping | Only a shout for help | Only the sound of a dog barking
